WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.500
Week eight.

00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:03.280
Creating advertising that works,

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:04.495
with Andrew Baxter,

00:00:04.545 --> 00:00:05.981
chair of Australian Pork,

00:00:06.031 --> 00:00:08.162
after twenty six years in agencies.

00:00:08.212 --> 00:00:09.318
His opener?

00:00:09.368 --> 00:00:12.154
Advertising is like selling fresh air.

00:00:12.867 --> 00:00:15.128
He ran Ogilvy and Publicis.

00:00:15.178 --> 00:00:17.357
His advice: pick your side.

00:00:17.407 --> 00:00:23.201
Agency life jumps around, marketing management goes deep, and consulting sits in between.

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:26.680
Ad vertere is Latin for turn the mind toward.

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:28.626
Posters go back to Pompeii.

00:00:28.676 --> 00:00:35.194
Since then, the town crier, newspapers, radio, TV, the internet and social.

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:37.572
Go where the eyeballs are.

00:00:37.622 --> 00:00:39.187
It used to be TV.

00:00:39.237 --> 00:00:40.626
Now it's the phone.

00:00:40.676 --> 00:00:44.746
And today it's about eighty percent science, twenty percent art.

00:00:45.433 --> 00:00:47.647
Ads in Australia must be truthful.

00:00:47.697 --> 00:00:51.197
Fines run past a million dollars, so bring the receipts.

00:00:51.247 --> 00:00:52.047
Oddly,

00:00:51.895 --> 00:00:53.190
politics is exempt,

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:56.391
because a court ruled there must be a financial outcome.

00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:00.953
Daniel Kahneman showed about ninety five percent of purchases are intuitive.

00:01:01.003 --> 00:01:02.144
We buy first,

00:01:02.194 --> 00:01:03.559
then post rationalise,

00:01:03.609 --> 00:01:06.378
and rational ads mostly help us do that.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:09.423
The Effie awards link ads to sales.

00:01:09.473 --> 00:01:11.298
But success can backfire.

00:01:11.348 --> 00:01:15.793
Lamb ads worked so well that people think lamb is only for Australia Day.

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:21.674
Advertising is simple: right message, right person, right place, right time.

00:01:21.724 --> 00:01:24.504
KFC and McDonald's switch screens by the hour,

00:01:24.554 --> 00:01:25.625
tradies at three,

00:01:25.675 --> 00:01:27.434
families at six.

00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:30.276
Making an ad takes four steps.

00:01:30.326 --> 00:01:35.500
Strategy, the idea, making it, which doesn't always work out, and placing it.

00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:40.171
Strategy is just ten percent of an agency, yet everyone wants in.

00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:42.940
You get fifteen words or less.

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:43.824
A billboard gets a two second glance.

00:01:43.874 --> 00:01:48.977
And use one message per ad, like powerful wash in cold water.

00:01:49.027 --> 00:01:50.937
Don't get too clever.

00:01:51.633 --> 00:01:52.609
Ads move people down a funnel: awareness, liking, preference, conviction, purchase.

00:01:52.659 --> 00:02:01.919
Aim to reach about sixty five percent of your audience at least three times.

00:02:02.633 --> 00:02:06.781
Kraft Easy Mac sold to mums, for teenage boys who get home hungry.

00:02:06.831 --> 00:02:09.682
The message: fills them up, fast to make.

00:02:09.732 --> 00:02:13.615
Kill hunger fast became the hunger blaster when the client balked.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:18.719
The most effective ads are famous, with seventy two percent outselling rivals.

00:02:18.769 --> 00:02:22.068
Emotional, successful sixty two percent of the time.

00:02:22.118 --> 00:02:24.610
And single minded and memorable.

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:27.349
Differentiation matters most.

00:02:27.399 --> 00:02:29.413
While Christmas ads all looked alike,

00:02:29.463 --> 00:02:31.205
John Lewis made Monty the Penguin,

00:02:31.255 --> 00:02:32.290
pure emotion.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:33.140
A hundred and thirty two million pounds in extra sales,

00:02:32.753 --> 00:02:37.530
and eight to one ROI.

00:02:38.233 --> 00:02:39.917
AI now helps with research,

00:02:39.967 --> 00:02:41.355
synthetic audiences,

00:02:41.405 --> 00:02:43.490
and many versions of content to test.

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:46.671
Nine in ten marketing teams already use it.

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:50.359
Marketing mix models show which channels worked together.

00:02:50.409 --> 00:02:52.859
Winning campaigns average ten point two.

00:02:52.909 --> 00:02:55.867
Digital now takes about sixty percent of media spend,

00:02:55.917 --> 00:02:56.916
led by Google,

00:02:56.966 --> 00:02:58.805
Meta and Amazon.

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:02.540
John Singleton said advertising exists to sell.

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:03.577
Mostly, but sometimes it's to change behaviour.

00:03:03.627 --> 00:03:08.943
So keep it simple, emotional and single minded.

00:03:08.993 --> 00:03:10.004
Make famous work that works.

00:03:10.054 --> 00:03:12.690
That's week eight.
